-- ===== begin itemasylum-hub.luau =====
--!nocheck
--[[
	SHADEEDWARE — Item Asylum
	Aimlock · Player ESP · Melee Fast Attack + Reach · Speed · Noclip

	Read out of the live client (IA: Main Game, place version 710):
	  players  -> plain Humanoid characters in workspace, R6; Teams only exist in team modes
	  melee    -> Tools whose Config (Configuration) carries a swing stat -- SwingSpeed or
	              M1SwingSpeed -- next to Cooldown and Damage. The swing runs in the tool's Server
	              script off Tool.Activated; the Client script only answers InvokeRemote with the
	              mouse position. The cooldown is enforced server-side, so fast attack re-sends
	              activation and lands every swing on the first frame the server allows one. It
	              can't go under the cooldown.
	  guns     -> Tools with the FIREBUTTON attribute. Their fire logic lives in the Client
	              script, so fast attack leaves them alone.
	  camera   -> Classic / Custom; holding a gun locks the cursor to the screen centre, which is
	              why Camera is the default aim method

	SETUP: none when run through shadeedware-loader.luau -- the loader carries the images.
	       Run on its own, the icon falls back to your Roblox headshot.
--]]

-- ICON_FILE is a local file in the executor's workspace ROOT (AppData\Local\Potassium\workspace).
-- Potassium's getcustomasset only resolves files at that root -- a subfolder path returns a
-- URL that silently decodes to 0x0 -- so keep the image there rather than in a folder.
-- The loader fills SHADEEDWARE_ICONS with one workspace file per bundled picture. Each picture needs
-- its own filename: Roblox caches a getcustomasset URL for the whole session, so overwriting one
-- file keeps showing the first image.
