-- ===== begin bedwars-hub.luau =====
--!nocheck
--[[
	SHADEEDWARE — BedWars
	Projectile Aimlock · FOV circle · Lock keys

	Read out of the live BedWars client (Game Mega, place version 4150):
	  launch   -> every item projectile -- bows, crossbows, headhunter, fireballs, snowballs, kit
	              throwables -- asks ProjectileController:calculateImportantLaunchValues for
	              { initialVelocity, positionFrom, deltaT, gravitationalAcceleration }. The module
	              (PlayerScripts.TS.controllers.global.combat.projectile.projectile-controller)
	              exports the live controller; the method sits on the class behind its metatable
	  flight   -> ProjectileUtil.fireProjectile spawns the model at positionFrom * CFrame(0.8, -0.6, 0)
	              in the launch frame, and a BodyForce leaves exactly gravitationalAcceleration of
	              fall. No drag, so the arc is a plain parabola
	  hits     -> the shooter's own client finds the hit and reports ProjectileHit(id, entity)
	  players  -> R15, HipHeight 2, root 2x2x1, a Team attribute on every player
	  keys     -> BedWars binds both Ctrl keys to shift lock, so the menu key here is Right Shift

	SETUP: none when run through shadeedware-loader.luau -- the loader carries the images.
	       Run on its own, it reads the manifest the loader left in the workspace; with neither,
	       the icon falls back to your Roblox headshot.
--]]

-- ICON_FILE is a local file in the executor's workspace ROOT (AppData\Local\Potassium\workspace).
-- Potassium's getcustomasset only resolves files at that root -- a subfolder path returns a
-- URL that silently decodes to 0x0 -- so keep the image there rather than in a folder.
-- The loader fills SHADEEDWARE_ICONS with one workspace file per bundled picture. Each picture needs
-- its own filename: Roblox caches a getcustomasset URL for the whole session, so overwriting one
-- file keeps showing the first image.
local ICON_RNG = Random.new()
local ICON_POOL = type(SHADEEDWARE_ICONS) == "table" and #SHADEEDWARE_ICONS > 0 and SHADEEDWARE_ICONS or { "shadeed.jpg" }
local ICON_FILE = ICON_POOL[1] -- swapped for the next pick in the cycle once glob exists
local VIDEO_POOL = type(SHADEEDWARE_VIDEOS) == "table" and SHADEEDWARE_VIDEOS or {}
-- controller-only extras (the loader's assets/remote): never in a rotation, shown only on request
local REMOTE_POOL = type(SHADEEDWARE_REMOTE) == "table" and SHADEEDWARE_REMOTE or { images = {}, anims = {} }
local ICON_ID = "" -- optional rbxassetid:// override, wins over ICON_FILE

----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- services
